WEBVTT

00:00:00.638 --> 00:00:03.758
In this guide we will set up the optional RoonPilot

00:00:03.650 --> 00:00:08.032
IR Bridge You will see every important click learn commands

00:00:07.925 --> 00:00:10.382
from your remote and assign the Bridge to a Roon

00:00:10.275 --> 00:00:15.070
zone No programming knowledge is needed Pause the video whenever

00:00:14.962 --> 00:00:16.920
you want to follow a step yourself

00:00:18.846 --> 00:00:24.066
Most importantly RoonPilot works without this Bridge Playback track

00:00:23.958 --> 00:00:28.378
selection Live Radio and volume control provided by Roon remain

00:00:28.271 --> 00:00:31.641
available You only need the IR Bridge if you also

00:00:31.533 --> 00:00:34.941
want to control equipment through its infrared remote such as

00:00:34.833 --> 00:00:37.878
an amplifier without suitable Roon volume control

00:00:39.750 --> 00:00:43.295
RoonPilot sends a control command to the Bridge over Bluetooth

00:00:43.488 --> 00:00:47.145
or over Wi-Fi when fallback is configured The Bridge then

00:00:47.038 --> 00:00:50.545
transmits the infrared command it learned earlier to your audio

00:00:50.438 --> 00:00:55.682
equipment This enables volume mute and optional power control The

00:00:55.575 --> 00:00:59.008
Bridge receiver is used to learn from the original remote

00:01:00.929 --> 00:01:04.249
The Bridge does not stream music replace a Roon Server

00:01:04.142 --> 00:01:07.224
or act as an audio endpoint It is not an

00:01:07.117 --> 00:01:10.737
RME MIDI Bridge or the Companion firmware inside the round

00:01:10.629 --> 00:01:15.412
device Ordinary infrared equipment does not report its actual volume

00:01:15.304 --> 00:01:19.612
or power state back Play pause and track changes still

00:01:19.504 --> 00:01:20.387
go to Roon

00:01:22.292 --> 00:01:24.649
For the documented reference unit you need an

00:01:24.542 --> 00:01:30.549
ESP32-S3-Zero-compatible board a suitable IR transmitter and an IR

00:01:30.442 --> 00:01:34.412
receiver for learning This guide shows an Adafruit High Power

00:01:34.304 --> 00:01:38.774
IR Emitter and a KY-022 receiver You also need a

00:01:38.667 --> 00:01:42.912
USB data cable and the original remote Check the exact

00:01:42.804 --> 00:01:45.212
board name not just its appearance

00:01:47.112 --> 00:01:51.808
Unplug USB before changing any wiring The transmitter signal

00:01:51.700 --> 00:01:57.170
connects to GPIO 4 also labelled GP4 The receiver output

00:01:57.062 --> 00:02:02.133
connects to GPIO 5 Connect the ground terminals to GND

00:02:02.412 --> 00:02:07.808
The documented receiver uses 3.3 volts Follow the module labels

00:02:07.950 --> 00:02:11.758
never cable colours alone Never apply 5 volts to a

00:02:11.650 --> 00:02:12.733
GPIO

00:02:14.638 --> 00:02:18.082
The Adafruit transmitter shown accepts a 3 to 5 volt

00:02:17.975 --> 00:02:22.695
supply and a 3.3 volt control signal Usable range also

00:02:22.588 --> 00:02:26.945
depends on its supply Beware a board label saying 5V

00:02:26.838 --> 00:02:31.282
does not guarantee a USB-powered output Check your particular board

00:02:31.175 --> 00:02:35.520
version and module terminals Do not connect two power sources

00:02:35.412 --> 00:02:39.882
together indiscriminately If unsure have the wiring checked

00:02:41.767 --> 00:02:44.949
Place the Bridge so its IR transmitter can reach the

00:02:44.842 --> 00:02:48.924
equipment’s sensor A closed cabinet door or a covered sensor

00:02:48.817 --> 00:02:53.062
can prevent commands getting through The receiver must be accessible

00:02:52.954 --> 00:02:56.724
to the remote while learning Keep the antenna area clear

00:02:56.617 --> 00:03:00.724
and use stable USB power An enclosure must not shield

00:03:00.617 --> 00:03:03.274
the transmitter receiver or antenna

00:03:05.179 --> 00:03:08.537
With a new Bridge you can continue straight away On

00:03:08.429 --> 00:03:13.324
an existing Bridge factory installation erases its identity pairing

00:03:13.467 --> 00:03:18.437
Wi-Fi and local profiles First create a configuration backup under

00:03:18.329 --> 00:03:24.662
System in RoonPilot This saves the profile library but version 2.0.2

00:03:24.554 --> 00:03:28.774
does not restore Bluetooth keys You must pair again afterwards

00:03:29.042 --> 00:03:33.087
For routine future updates use the Bridge update in RoonPilot

00:03:32.979 --> 00:03:33.712
instead

00:03:35.612 --> 00:03:40.233
Install using current Chrome or Edge on a computer Firefox

00:03:40.325 --> 00:03:44.308
Safari iPhone and iPad are not suitable for this USB

00:03:44.200 --> 00:03:47.608
installer Later you can use a phone to configure the

00:03:47.500 --> 00:03:52.532
RoonPilot webpage Close any program using the serial USB port

00:03:52.425 --> 00:03:55.920
and use a data cable A charge-only cable is not

00:03:55.812 --> 00:03:56.458
enough

00:03:58.375 --> 00:04:02.158
For installation connect only this Bridge to the computer

00:04:02.400 --> 00:04:07.008
Temporarily disconnect other ESP32 devices from the computer

00:04:07.200 --> 00:04:11.382
including the round RoonPilot Both can show the same USB

00:04:11.275 --> 00:04:15.170
name On a factory-new board hold BOOT while plugging it

00:04:15.062 --> 00:04:18.258
in and release once the port appears The Bridge does

00:04:18.150 --> 00:04:22.082
not need the USB-C connector reversal used for the Companion

00:04:21.975 --> 00:04:23.632
inside the round device

00:04:25.529 --> 00:04:29.674
Open the official IR Bridge installer The correct link is

00:04:29.567 --> 00:04:33.874
directly below this video Check the Bridge factory installer heading

00:04:33.767 --> 00:04:38.112
and the address containing ir-bridge slash install Do not use

00:04:38.004 --> 00:04:41.799
the main firmware installer or the Companion installer We are

00:04:41.692 --> 00:04:45.124
installing only the firmware for the separate IR Bridge

00:04:47.054 --> 00:04:53.049
The release shown is IR Bridge 1.0.0 for RoonPilot 2.0.2

00:04:53.329 --> 00:04:56.624
The different numbers are correct these are separate firmware

00:04:56.517 --> 00:05:00.249
products In future the page may show a newer Bridge

00:05:00.142 --> 00:05:04.037
version What matters is using the correct Bridge installer and

00:05:03.929 --> 00:05:06.949
supported ESP32-S3 hardware

00:05:08.821 --> 00:05:12.928
Scroll to the installation section Read and confirm the three

00:05:12.821 --> 00:05:17.216
items covering hardware full erase and the licence Tick each

00:05:17.108 --> 00:05:21.491
box only when the statement actually applies Connect and install

00:05:21.383 --> 00:05:26.253
Bridge then becomes available This button first opens USB device

00:05:26.146 --> 00:05:29.591
selection It does not immediately write the firmware

00:05:31.488 --> 00:05:37.520
Select USB JTAG slash serial debug unit for the ESP32-S3

00:05:37.413 --> 00:05:41.945
Bridge board Windows shows a COM number macOS usually shows

00:05:41.838 --> 00:05:46.795
cu dot usbmodem The number or suffix varies between computers

00:05:47.038 --> 00:05:50.895
Click the correct row first then Connect With only the

00:05:50.788 --> 00:05:54.145
Bridge attached you cannot confuse it with RoonPilot

00:05:56.054 --> 00:05:59.224
If the entry only says USB serial it is not

00:05:59.117 --> 00:06:04.887
the documented native ESP32-S3 port Do not start an installation

00:06:04.779 --> 00:06:08.949
by guesswork Disconnect the wrong device and connect the correct

00:06:08.842 --> 00:06:13.537
Bridge board The open dialog updates its list Unlike the

00:06:13.429 --> 00:06:17.112
round Waveshare device reversing the Bridge connector does not

00:06:17.004 --> 00:06:18.662
select a second processor

00:06:20.554 --> 00:06:23.874
If no device appears try a known data cable and

00:06:23.767 --> 00:06:28.137
a direct computer port without a hub Unplug USB hold

00:06:28.029 --> 00:06:31.499
BOOT on the Bridge and plug USB back in Release

00:06:31.392 --> 00:06:35.262
BOOT when the native port appears Also check that another

00:06:35.154 --> 00:06:39.162
program is not using the port BOOT helps with installation

00:06:39.379 --> 00:06:42.037
it is not the normal Bluetooth pairing procedure

00:06:43.904 --> 00:06:49.399
After connecting the device dialog opens Choose Install RoonPilot IR

00:06:49.292 --> 00:06:53.487
Bridge The installation tool may use English labels even on

00:06:53.379 --> 00:06:57.487
the German webpage That is normal In the next step

00:06:57.379 --> 00:07:00.412
we explicitly select the full erase of the Bridge

00:07:02.267 --> 00:07:06.074
Tick Erase device in the dialog and click Next This

00:07:05.967 --> 00:07:10.699
prepares a full factory installation An existing Bridge loses its

00:07:10.592 --> 00:07:14.312
old identity and setup You do not need a separate

00:07:14.204 --> 00:07:18.812
erase beforehand The separate RoonPilot device remains untouched

00:07:18.967 --> 00:07:21.624
provided you selected the correct Bridge as shown

00:07:23.488 --> 00:07:27.570
In the confirmation dialog check the RoonPilot IR Bridge name

00:07:27.463 --> 00:07:31.433
and erase warning once more Install now starts the actual

00:07:31.325 --> 00:07:36.008
process Keep the USB cable connected the browser open and

00:07:35.900 --> 00:07:39.920
the computer awake Do not interrupt power or press BOOT

00:07:39.813 --> 00:07:41.058
during installation

00:07:42.971 --> 00:07:46.916
The installer prepares the connection erases flash storage and then

00:07:46.808 --> 00:07:51.066
writes the firmware The percentage may increase at different speeds

00:07:51.346 --> 00:07:54.928
Wait for the completion message not just a single display

00:07:54.821 --> 00:07:58.703
of one hundred percent This waiting period is shortened in

00:07:58.596 --> 00:08:02.641
the video Installation may take longer on your computer

00:08:04.517 --> 00:08:09.199
Installation complete means the process has finished Choose Next and

00:08:09.092 --> 00:08:12.762
close the dialog The Bridge starts with a new RPB

00:08:12.654 --> 00:08:17.162
identity and slowly pulses blue Leave it on stable USB

00:08:17.054 --> 00:08:21.524
power Unlike RoonPilot this IR Bridge does not open its

00:08:21.417 --> 00:08:25.599
own setup Wi-Fi Continue on your RoonPilot webpage

00:08:27.500 --> 00:08:31.220
RoonPilot must already be configured for your home Wi-Fi and

00:08:31.112 --> 00:08:35.883
Roon If not follow the separate RoonPilot video guide first

00:08:36.150 --> 00:08:39.658
Now open its local webpage using the known IP address

00:08:39.550 --> 00:08:43.782
and choose IR Bridge Newer interfaces may call this simply

00:08:43.675 --> 00:08:47.958
Bridges Keep RoonPilot and the Bridge close together for initial

00:08:47.850 --> 00:08:48.520
pairing

00:08:50.429 --> 00:08:53.287
If Bridge and Bluetooth is off switch it on and

00:08:53.179 --> 00:08:57.112
choose Save and restart Confirm the restart and wait for

00:08:57.004 --> 00:09:01.399
RoonPilot to become reachable again Only then is Bluetooth actually

00:09:01.292 --> 00:09:05.462
running An enabled switch without the required restart is not

00:09:05.354 --> 00:09:10.149
enough Reopen the Bridge page afterwards If Bluetooth is already

00:09:10.042 --> 00:09:12.812
active you do not need to enable it again

00:09:14.683 --> 00:09:19.428
Choose Scan for Bridges Compare the complete RPB identity of

00:09:19.321 --> 00:09:23.178
your new Bridge with the discovered entry The identity shown

00:09:23.071 --> 00:09:26.678
is only an example Do not simply choose the strongest

00:09:26.571 --> 00:09:31.391
signal if several Bridges appear Later Identify Bridge can flash

00:09:31.283 --> 00:09:33.866
a brief blue signal to help you match the correct

00:09:33.758 --> 00:09:34.516
enclosure

00:09:36.392 --> 00:09:40.662
Choose Pair this Bridge beside the correct identity Wait until

00:09:40.554 --> 00:09:44.937
the secure connection is ready Successful pairing is confirmed by

00:09:44.829 --> 00:09:49.312
two brief blue LED flashes Security should show an encrypted

00:09:49.204 --> 00:09:53.562
and bonded connection A Bridge cannot belong to several RoonPilot

00:09:53.454 --> 00:09:55.249
devices at the same time

00:09:57.100 --> 00:10:01.358
Check the saved Bridge and choose Test connection This confirms

00:10:01.250 --> 00:10:05.370
communication between RoonPilot and the Bridge not yet its effect

00:10:05.262 --> 00:10:08.370
on the amplifier You can give the Bridge a useful

00:10:08.262 --> 00:10:12.608
display name Its LED normally stays off during idle operation

00:10:12.812 --> 00:10:14.932
that is intentional not a fault

00:10:16.808 --> 00:10:20.991
For greater range you can allow Wi-Fi fallback Select the

00:10:20.883 --> 00:10:24.541
intended Bridge using Manage and stay within Bluetooth range

00:10:24.433 --> 00:10:29.116
initially RoonPilot sends its saved Wi-Fi credentials to the Bridge

00:10:29.008 --> 00:10:33.478
over the encrypted connection Wait for the 2.4 gigahertz network

00:10:33.371 --> 00:10:37.266
connection and test the Wi-Fi path Then return to zone

00:10:37.158 --> 00:10:41.841
control No separate Bridge setup Wi-Fi or additional webpage is

00:10:41.733 --> 00:10:42.378
needed

00:10:44.279 --> 00:10:47.499
An IR profile groups the commands for one piece of

00:10:47.392 --> 00:10:52.699
audio equipment Open IR profiles and choose Create profile Give

00:10:52.592 --> 00:10:56.437
it a unique name such as Living Room Amplifier This

00:10:56.329 --> 00:11:00.599
library is saved on RoonPilot It is independent of which

00:11:00.492 --> 00:11:03.212
Bridge eventually sends the commands in each room

00:11:05.125 --> 00:11:08.820
Start with a carrier frequency of 38 kilohertz and a

00:11:08.713 --> 00:11:14.233
duty cycle of 33 percent These suit many remotes Duty cycle

00:11:14.125 --> 00:11:17.683
does not mean volume or the number of repeats Change

00:11:17.575 --> 00:11:20.783
these values only when your equipment is known to require

00:11:20.675 --> 00:11:25.508
something different Choose Save on RoonPilot The new profile

00:11:25.400 --> 00:11:27.633
initially has no learned commands

00:11:29.529 --> 00:11:33.387
Choose the saved profile and under Learning Bridge the paired

00:11:33.279 --> 00:11:37.724
Bridge that has an IR receiver Click Start learning Normal

00:11:37.617 --> 00:11:41.449
IR transmission is locked during this session If you have

00:11:41.342 --> 00:11:45.512
several Bridges one receiver is enough to learn all profiles

00:11:45.792 --> 00:11:48.962
The Bridge used for transmission later can be a different

00:11:48.854 --> 00:11:49.312
one

00:11:51.208 --> 00:11:55.203
Start with Volume down and choose Learn beside it Wait

00:11:55.096 --> 00:11:58.728
for First recording Point the original remote at the Bridge

00:11:58.621 --> 00:12:02.153
receiver from about ten to thirty centimetres away not at

00:12:02.046 --> 00:12:06.053
the round RoonPilot display Press the appropriate button as you

00:12:05.946 --> 00:12:08.041
normally would then release it

00:12:09.929 --> 00:12:13.537
Wait for Second recording and press exactly the same remote

00:12:13.429 --> 00:12:18.024
button again The Bridge compares both captures On success the

00:12:17.917 --> 00:12:21.299
command is marked Captured and the LED confirms in green

00:12:21.579 --> 00:12:24.374
If there is an error repeat with the same button

00:12:24.267 --> 00:12:27.937
and better alignment Do not press another button between the

00:12:27.829 --> 00:12:28.899
two captures

00:12:30.779 --> 00:12:34.937
Also learn Volume up Mute and if needed Power on

00:12:34.829 --> 00:12:38.937
and Power off On and off deliberately have separate slots

00:12:39.217 --> 00:12:42.149
If your remote uses the same button learn it into

00:12:42.042 --> 00:12:45.562
both slots this does not create genuine separate on and

00:12:45.454 --> 00:12:49.612
off codes If switching off needs a held press reproduce

00:12:49.504 --> 00:12:53.849
that behaviour Later enable only functions whose commands you

00:12:53.742 --> 00:12:54.862
actually learned

00:12:56.725 --> 00:13:01.320
After recording choose Save on RoonPilot This is what commits

00:13:01.213 --> 00:13:04.570
the confirmed commands to the persistent library and ends the

00:13:04.463 --> 00:13:09.045
learning session Discard keeps the previous library version instead

00:13:09.300 --> 00:13:13.758
An unfinished session expires after at most ten minutes Test

00:13:13.650 --> 00:13:17.258
the commands only after saving and completing the following zone

00:13:17.150 --> 00:13:17.995
assignment

00:13:19.863 --> 00:13:23.908
Open Zone routing and find the intended Roon zone Choose

00:13:23.800 --> 00:13:27.858
External IR Bridge then the correct Bridge and learned profile

00:13:28.100 --> 00:13:32.845
Click Save RoonPilot automatically transfers and verifies the

00:13:32.738 --> 00:13:37.158
required profile copy before activating the route Other zones can

00:13:37.050 --> 00:13:41.383
continue using normal Roon volume control If the target Bridge

00:13:41.275 --> 00:13:45.570
is unreachable a new route is not activated without verification

00:13:47.446 --> 00:13:51.366
Set the knob step under Zone Management Start with one

00:13:51.258 --> 00:13:55.666
times Two times sends two IR volume commands per detent

00:13:55.833 --> 00:14:00.428
not automatically two decibels Enable Power and Mute separately for

00:14:00.321 --> 00:14:04.191
the zone but only with the corresponding learned commands A

00:14:04.083 --> 00:14:07.266
short tap on Power means on a long press means

00:14:07.158 --> 00:14:10.666
off Playback and pause remain Roon controls

00:14:12.558 --> 00:14:15.466
Pause playback and set a low level on the audio

00:14:15.358 --> 00:14:19.666
equipment Select the assigned zone on RoonPilot and first turn

00:14:19.558 --> 00:14:23.478
down by just one detent Watch the equipment does its

00:14:23.371 --> 00:14:28.191
volume change RoonPilot displays IR Volume with a relative step

00:14:28.083 --> 00:14:31.866
value This is not a volume reading from the amplifier

00:14:32.121 --> 00:14:36.616
Only then test volume up mute and carefully optional power

00:14:36.508 --> 00:14:37.253
commands

00:14:39.167 --> 00:14:42.937
Slow blue means the pairing window is open Two brief

00:14:42.829 --> 00:14:47.462
blue flashes confirm pairing Orange accompanies learning two green

00:14:47.354 --> 00:14:51.162
flashes confirm a matching capture and two red flashes indicate

00:14:51.054 --> 00:14:55.224
a learning error Violet is used during firmware updates do

00:14:55.117 --> 00:14:59.499
not disconnect power then During normal idle operation the LED

00:14:59.392 --> 00:15:03.599
is off Read the ongoing connection status on the RoonPilot

00:15:03.492 --> 00:15:04.149
page

00:15:06.054 --> 00:15:09.162
If the equipment does not respond first check the Bridge

00:15:09.054 --> 00:15:13.874
connection selected zone profile and transmitter alignment A

00:15:13.767 --> 00:15:18.424
successful connection test does not prove IR reception To re-pair

00:15:18.317 --> 00:15:22.487
a previously paired Bridge deliberately power-cycle it three times

00:15:22.379 --> 00:15:26.999
within fifteen seconds Then use its five-minute blue pairing window

00:15:27.279 --> 00:15:31.799
This is not a routine restart procedure Shared USB chargers

00:15:31.692 --> 00:15:34.724
can briefly interrupt other connected devices too

00:15:36.613 --> 00:15:41.320
RoonPilot can save up to four IR Bridges Deliberately assign

00:15:41.213 --> 00:15:45.133
each zone its Bridge and profile Manage selects a Bridge

00:15:45.025 --> 00:15:48.683
for configuration or maintenance it does not simply change the

00:15:48.575 --> 00:15:52.195
route for your music zone Return to zone control after

00:15:52.088 --> 00:15:56.533
maintenance Start with one Bridge you can add other transmitters

00:15:56.425 --> 00:15:57.033
later

00:15:58.929 --> 00:16:03.099
When everything works create a new configuration backup under System

00:16:02.992 --> 00:16:06.712
and store the file privately on your computer This saves

00:16:06.604 --> 00:16:12.437
profiles and routing After a full erase version 2.0.2 requires

00:16:12.329 --> 00:16:16.887
pairing again first then restoring the appropriate profiles Start

00:16:16.779 --> 00:16:20.774
future Bridge updates manually under Maintenance in RoonPilot

00:16:21.042 --> 00:16:25.674
Routine application updates preserve setup both devices must remain

00:16:25.567 --> 00:16:26.737
powered during them

00:16:28.638 --> 00:16:32.695
Your optional IR Bridge is now installed paired and assigned

00:16:32.588 --> 00:16:36.208
to a zone Roon still handles the music the Bridge

00:16:36.100 --> 00:16:40.783
adds learned equipment commands RoonPilot continues working without

00:16:40.675 --> 00:16:44.808
a Bridge Use the chapters to revisit any step The

00:16:44.700 --> 00:16:48.458
written guides and official installer are linked below the video
